{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00204",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 3.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Good morning, how are you doing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.06,
      "end_seconds": 7.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. It's been a long few days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 8.35,
      "end_seconds": 12.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Hmm, doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.42,
      "end_seconds": 18.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them. Is this your first time with this clinic?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.53,
      "end_seconds": 25.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Mm, you know, first time with this one, yes. A friend recommended it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.85,
      "end_seconds": 27.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "So, what's been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 28.62,
      "end_seconds": 32.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "She's been having red scaly patches on my elbows, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.18,
      "end_seconds": 40.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.92,
      "end_seconds": 45.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "So, it's been about a year, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.21,
      "end_seconds": 54.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "Okay, can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.92,
      "end_seconds": 61.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Yes, cold weather. That makes it worse. I get some relief from sunlight. Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.76,
      "end_seconds": 66.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.81,
      "end_seconds": 75.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Itching goes along with it, most of the time. The itching? That's been for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.48,
      "end_seconds": 79.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Have you had stiff fingers in the morning?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.87,
      "end_seconds": 83.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.98,
      "end_seconds": 91.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.39,
      "end_seconds": 93.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.0,
      "end_seconds": 96.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Has there been any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.89,
      "end_seconds": 101.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "No, uh, I haven't had any fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 101.35,
      "end_seconds": 106.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.57,
      "end_seconds": 112.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.14,
      "end_seconds": 123.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Alright, any joint swelling, sore throat before it started, new medicines or weeping?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.88,
      "end_seconds": 126.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.34,
      "end_seconds": 131.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.89,
      "end_seconds": 134.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.33,
      "end_seconds": 138.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Okay, what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.22,
      "end_seconds": 141.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.34,
      "end_seconds": 144.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Let me just write this down properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.52,
      "end_seconds": 163.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Okay, continuing. What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 164.07,
      "end_seconds": 166.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "So, it's coconut oil, daily, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.23,
      "end_seconds": 170.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.08,
      "end_seconds": 173.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.34,
      "end_seconds": 180.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.04,
      "end_seconds": 183.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.01,
      "end_seconds": 187.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.05,
      "end_seconds": 188.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.07,
      "end_seconds": 206.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.32,
      "end_seconds": 226.62,
      "duration_seconds": 19.3,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about ten years. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I've had diabetes, yes. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.01,
      "end_seconds": 234.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.37,
      "end_seconds": 250.35,
      "duration_seconds": 11.98,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.7,
      "end_seconds": 252.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.8,
      "end_seconds": 257.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I had a hernia repair about five years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.21,
      "end_seconds": 262.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.71,
      "end_seconds": 267.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.18,
      "end_seconds": 273.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Okay, anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.93,
      "end_seconds": 275.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "My father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.25,
      "end_seconds": 281.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.57,
      "end_seconds": 296.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.75,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.7,
      "end_seconds": 299.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.89,
      "end_seconds": 303.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Uh, it's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.05,
      "end_seconds": 308.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.46,
      "end_seconds": 312.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.09,
      "end_seconds": 324.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Well-defined thick silvery plaques over both elbows and knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.5,
      "end_seconds": 328.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.23,
      "end_seconds": 342.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "A few small pits in the fingernails."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.71,
      "end_seconds": 344.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.53,
      "end_seconds": 365.46,
      "duration_seconds": 14.93,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.82,
      "end_seconds": 369.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.27,
      "end_seconds": 382.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.88,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with plaque psoriasis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep eczema in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.7,
      "end_seconds": 384.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.49,
      "end_seconds": 403.79,
      "duration_seconds": 18.3,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like plaque psoriasis, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had red scaly patches on your elbows for about a year, mild, and no joint swelling or sore throat before it started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.26,
      "end_seconds": 406.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.12,
      "end_seconds": 411.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.08,
      "end_seconds": 415.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.57,
      "end_seconds": 439.7,
      "duration_seconds": 24.13,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for baseline before treatment. I'd like you to take calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day, for four weeks. That's for psoriasis. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. A little sunlight helps psoriasis, but avoid sunburn. Moisturise often. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 440.74,
      "end_seconds": 450.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. We'll refer you to a dermatologist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 451.8,
      "end_seconds": 452.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.75,
      "end_seconds": 462.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 463.21,
      "end_seconds": 465.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Yeah, yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.93,
      "end_seconds": 468.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Come back in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 469.8,
      "end_seconds": 471.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 472.23,
      "end_seconds": 477.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 477.99,
      "end_seconds": 485.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "So, I take the calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 487.04,
      "end_seconds": 491.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0075",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 492.36,
      "end_seconds": 495.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I, I appreciate your time, doctor."
    }
  ]
}